From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:50:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 042/260] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the shorter
 usage popover and light tooltips

The review of patches 0040 and 0041 (2026-10-14: Codex found nothing,
Claude's /code-review found four things Reid asked to fix):

- Shortcut tooltips (KeyboardShortcutTooltipContent) still forced a
  near-black slate chip, so in light mode one button could show a dark
  shortcut tooltip beside a light error tooltip. They now take the popover
  surface like every other tooltip, with the default Kbd chips.
- The "Couldn't update configuration" tooltip kept its own border and also
  got the new base ring, so it drew two outlines; its border is gone.
- From 60 percent used the context bar is one amber or red fill, and a
  stale reading draws it grey, but the legend kept its blue, green and grey
  dots. The legend now drops its dots whenever the bar is not drawn in the
  segment colors.
- A plan explainer opened while the popover was still loading closed
  itself when the data arrived. Its open state now lives in the panel.

ChatPage.composer.test.tsx gains a file-wide stand-in for AeTeamControl,
which needs a QueryClient and the sidebar data provider since patch 0030.
Without it the suite's config-error test could not run, and 296 other
tests in that file had been failing unseen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
